  "question": {
    "text": "An object is dropped from a height&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math> from the ground. Every time it hits the ground it loses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of its kinetic energy. The total distance covered as <math><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>&#8734;</mi></math> is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>3</mn><mi>h</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>∞</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>h</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>h</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Since the object is dropped from height, thus its potential energy is equal to its kinetic energy.</p><p>As per question, kinetic energy after hitting the ground is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>&#8242;</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><br /><br /><math><msup><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#8242;</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mi>u</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br />The total distance covered<math><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>h</mi></math></p>"
  }
}